/-!
# Characteristic-ℓ Frobenius and Hecke operators on modular function fields

Definition: `ModularCurve_CharLFrobeniusGeomLevel` (`ab79ccd6-b062-520c-a291-c05b75df1a27`), by
Claude, 2026-09-05.

Fix a field $K$ of characteristic $\ell$ ($\ell$ prime), an integer $N \neq 0$, a datum `data :
ModularPolynomialData ℓ` and a hypothesis `hKr : KroneckerCongruence ℓ data`. Inside $K((q))$ the
field `modularFunctionFieldC K N` is the intermediate field generated over $K$ by `jqModC K` (the
Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the reduction of the integral power series `jNum`, i.e. the
$q$-expansion of $j$) and by `jqNModC K N`, its image under the substitution $q \mapsto q^N$. The
substitution $q \mapsto q^\ell$, packaged as a $K$-algebra endomorphism `qExpandAlgC K ℓ` of
$K((q))$, raises each of these two generators to the $\ell$-th power, by the identity $j(q^\ell) =
j(q)^\ell$ recorded in `ModularPolynomialData.frobenius_identity_geom`; hence it maps the field into
itself, and `frobeniusGeomLevel` is the resulting injective $K$-algebra endomorphism, with
`frobeniusGeomLevelImage` its image and `frobeniusGeomLevelEquiv` the isomorphism onto that image.
Every $\ell$-th power lies in the image, so the extension is purely inseparable of exponent dividing
$\ell$: `isFrobeniusEndo_frobeniusGeomLevel` verifies both clauses of `IsFrobeniusEndo ℓ`, namely
that each $x^\ell$ is a value and each value is an $\ell$-th power, given that $K$ is closed under
$\ell$-th roots.

On places, `frobOnPlacesGeomLevel` sends $w$ to the place whose valuation subring consists of the
$x$ with `frobeniusGeomLevel x` in that of $w$; it is injective, and surjective under the same
perfectness hypothesis, via `IsFrobeniusEndo.extendPlace`, which pulls a place back along the ring
homomorphism `frobNormRingHom` given by the inverse-image map `frobNorm`. `verOnPlacesGeomLevel` is
a classically chosen one-sided inverse. Ramification is computed: $\mathrm{ord}_w(\mathrm{Frob}\,g)
= \ell\,\mathrm{ord}_{\mathrm{Frob}(w)}(g)$.

On divisors, `frobeniusPushforwardGeomLevel` transports supports along `frobOnPlacesGeomLevel`,
`frobeniusPullbackGeomLevel` sends $\langle v, n\rangle$ to $\langle \mathrm{Ver}(v), n\ell\rangle$,
and `heckeFibreGeomLevel` is their sum. Their composite satisfies $\mathrm{Frob}^*\mathrm{Frob}_* =
\ell$, degrees are multiplied by $1$, $\ell$ and $\ell+1$ when all places have degree one, and all
three preserve principality; they therefore descend to degree-zero divisors and to `Pic0`, where
`eichlerShimura_special_fibre_pic0_level` gives $\mathrm{Frob}_*^2 - T\,\mathrm{Frob}_* + \ell = 0$.
The `…OfIsCurveOver` variants supply the perfectness and degree-one hypotheses from $K$
algebraically closed together with `IsCurveOver K (modularFunctionFieldC K N)`.

**Relation to Mathlib.** The framework of places, divisors, degree-zero divisors and `Pic0` for a
function field, the predicate `IsCurveOver`, and `IsFrobeniusEndo` are the project's own; Mathlib
supplies the ambient `LaurentSeries`, `IntermediateField`, `ValuationSubring` and `Finsupp`
material. Some general lemmas on valuation subrings and on ramification indices of restricted places
are proved here alongside.

**Where it is used.** These operators model the Frobenius and Verschiebung morphisms, and the Hecke
correspondence $T_\ell$, on the characteristic-$\ell$ fibre of the modular curve of level $N$, the
Eichler–Shimura congruence relation on its Jacobian being what links Hecke eigenvalues to traces of
Frobenius in the Galois representations attached to modular forms.

